  "lineage": "Senegalese Wolof sabar drumming tradition, the canonical drum-language and ceremonial-dance percussion-form of Senegal and The Gambia. The sabar ensemble centers on the open-bottomed wood-and-hide sabar drum played with curved stick in right hand and bare left hand, with several drum-types (nder lead, mbung-mbung mid, tugne low, gorong bottom) constructing polyrhythmic dialogue. The bakk drum-language is a quasi-linguistic communication system encoding named messages. Doudou N'Diaye Rose consolidated the contemporary repertoire and trained the largest performing ensemble.",
